WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.430
The first live-action Justice League was always
going to feature lots of plot development

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.740
to properly establish a team-up between DC
Comics legends.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.790
But with its four-hour-runtime, Zack Snyder's
Justice League is jam-packed with world building

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.200
heading into its final act.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.910
"Isn't that right … Batman?"

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.640
Here's the ending of the Snyder Cut, explained.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.470
Zack Snyder's Justice League is not short
on story.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.619
The film establishes the individual worlds
of newbie superheroes like Cyborg, Aquaman,

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:32.650
and the Flash, while also depicting a world
still reeling from the demise of Superman

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.510
at the end of Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.480
In these earlier scenes, Snyder and company
establish the personality traits of our superhero

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.640
protagonists that will end up being crucial
in the film's climax.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.510
For example, we're introduced to a forlorn
Cyborg, still unsure of what to do with his

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.070
new robotic enhancements.

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:52.030
Barry Allen, meanwhile, is stuck doing dead-end
jobs to help pursue a criminal law degree

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.140
so he can get his dad, Henry, out of prison.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.960
The individual members of the titular Justice
League have very different personal problems

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.960
to work out.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.870
However, a recurring trait across Cyborg and
Aquaman's storylines is a lack of interest

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.720
in working as a team player.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.000
Despite those doubts, all of these heroes
are forced to work together once Steppenwolf

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.580
begins assembling the Mother Boxes to destroy
Earth.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.070
It's a threat so intimidating that the team
decides to use one of the Mother Boxes to

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.400
resurrect Superman, a figure powerful enough
to help defeat this otherworldly entity.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.720
By the time the finale begins, the Justice
League has headed off to Russia to confront

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.810
their cosmic enemy, and Superman has come
back to life and is regaining his personality

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.860
by sharing tender moments with Lois Lane.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.270
Will this epic resurrection pay off in the
end?

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.270
"It has to."

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:36.500
Every member of the Justice League has a critical
role to play in the final confrontation against

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.740
Steppenwolf, and Barry Allen is no exception.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:43.030
In order for Cyborg to access the trio of
Mother Boxes, he'll require a shock of electricity

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:47.070
that can only be generated by the Flash running
at an incredibly high level of speed.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.700
While engaging in that kind of run, the Flash
is shot down by a Parademon soldier.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.890
With our hero briefly knocked aside, Darkseid
and his forces are given enough time to activate

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.850
the Mother Boxes and destroy Earth.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.770
But just as the planet is being annihilated,
the Flash decides to break his one rule and

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.479
run so fast that he ends up going back in
time.

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:07.440
It's a risky move that the superhero isn't
sure he'll be able to survive, but he has

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.429
no choice if he wants to save the world.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:13.260
While running at such an extreme velocity,
the Flash remembers his father's remark that

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.400
his son was "the best of the best," and Barry
realizes that he's finally lived up to that

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.400
moniker.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.319
In the end, his daunting run pays off enormously,
as time is turned back just enough so Flash

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:25.740
can give Cyborg that electrical boost, thus
cementing the world's safety.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.310
However, it also gives Barry Allen the revelation
that he is indeed capable of traveling through

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.450
time, an ability that's gotten the character
into plenty of trouble in comic book storylines

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.450
like Flashpoint.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.250
Much like in the theatrical cut of Justice
League, Zack Snyder's version sees Superman

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:44.140
returning from the dead, briefly turning evil,
and then restoring his original personality

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.830
just in time to stop Steppenwolf from destroying
Earth.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.800
In Snyder's version, though, the transition
takes longer to happen.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.870
The biggest deviation between the films is
an extended scene in Zack Snyder's Justice

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:57.900
League depicting Superman returning to his
Fortress of Solitude before he reunites with

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:58.900
the Justice League.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.459
The resurrected Kryptonian walks around the
halls of his lair while the voices of his

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:06.480
two fathers, Jor-El and Johnathan Kent, speak
to him about the importance of pursuing who

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.480
he wants to be.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.400
By the end of this sequence, Superman is wearing
a black version of his traditional superhero

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.920
suit, and he flies away, ready to join the
Justice League.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.890
When he does, he manages to get there just
in the nick of time.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.540
Steppenwolf's axe is about to land on Cyborg
when Superman intervenes.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.170
Using his superpowered breath to turn the
axe into ice, Superman makes his powerful

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.500
presence apparent, and he and Steppenwolf
proceed to have a duel.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:32.880
This confrontation ends with Superman pinning
the beast to the ground and punching him repeatedly.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.450
Superman returned to this world unsure of
where he stood or who he was.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:40.200
As he fights Steppenwolf for the good of humanity,
it becomes apparent that the Man of Steel

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.710
has become the protector he was always meant
to be.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:47.340
In the final battle against Steppenwolf's
forces, Cyborg takes it upon himself to disconnect

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.319
the three Mother Boxes, thus preventing Earth's
destruction.

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:54.400
His ability to tap into any piece of technology
means he has the best chance of dismantling

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.849
these objects and foiling Steppenwolf's plan.

00:03:56.849 --> 00:03:59.790
Wonder Woman makes it apparent, though, that
there is a risk to this.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:03.880
While Cyborg is tapping into them, the Mother
Boxes will exploit his fears in an attempt

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:04.880
to stop him.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.290
And that's just what happens once Cyborg gets
inside the Mother Boxes and sees a vision

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.080
of his parents, Silas and Elinore.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.440
They stand there with a fully healed version
of Cyborg and urge their son to stop fighting.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:18.620
It's a scenario designed to tap into Cyborg's
insecurities and stop him from disconnecting

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:19.669
those Mother Boxes.

00:04:19.669 --> 00:04:22.129
But our hero isn't backing down now.

00:04:22.129 --> 00:04:25.020
Cyborg continues his mission with the help
of his Justice League comrades.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.749
The young man who once sat in his apartment
alone and unsure of where he fit in this world

00:04:28.749 --> 00:04:33.169
has now come to accept his new form, his new
friends and his new purpose on the planet.

00:04:33.169 --> 00:04:36.770
It's also a sequence that fulfills earlier
rumors that Cyborg would be getting a much

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.120
greater spotlight in Zack Snyder's Justice
League.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.389
All of the members of the Justice League have
a bone to pick with Steppenwolf, given that

00:04:43.389 --> 00:04:45.849
he's keen on eradicating the planet they call
home.

00:04:45.849 --> 00:04:50.189
However, Wonder Woman develops her own personal
animosity with this Apokolips resident after

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.139
an intense mid-movie interaction.

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:56.080
Here, Steppenwolf reveals that he slaughtered
many of Wonder Woman's Amazonian allies in

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.879
his pursuit of the Mother Box that was once
held on the island.

00:04:58.879 --> 00:05:02.909
Enraged at the thought of Themyscira's finest
warriors dying at his hands, Wonder Woman's

00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:05.740
quest for revenge against Steppenwolf is initiated.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:10.740
Once the final battle arrives, Wonder Woman
leads Aquaman and Cyborg to a personal confrontation

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:11.740
with Steppenwolf.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.080
Here, the alien once again taunts Wonder Woman
with how many Amazonian's he's killed, all

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.599
the while reminding her that she could've
saved them if she hadn't abandoned her home

00:05:18.599 --> 00:05:20.169
for the world of man.

00:05:20.169 --> 00:05:23.949
Enraged, Wonder Woman begins to brutally fight
back against the villain and even bangs her

00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:27.669
bracelets on her shield to create an explosion
that sends Steppenwolf spinning.

00:05:27.669 --> 00:05:31.439
Eventually, after the other members of the
Justice League join in to fight this monster,

00:05:31.439 --> 00:05:32.919
Wonder Woman gets her revenge.

00:05:32.919 --> 00:05:36.779
The final move that kills this minion of Darkseid
is Wonder Woman slicing off his head with

00:05:36.779 --> 00:05:37.779
her sword.

00:05:37.779 --> 00:05:40.970
With the flick of a blade, Wonder Woman has
honored the memories of her fallen Amazonian

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:41.970
comrades.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.509
Zack Snyder's Justice League ends on many
teases of things to come, with one of those

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:48.089
involving Darkseid.

00:05:48.089 --> 00:05:51.849
Seen throughout the movie as the intimidating
superior and nephew of Steppenwolf, Darkseid

00:05:51.849 --> 00:05:54.809
has been firmly established as someone you
don't want to cross.

00:05:54.809 --> 00:05:59.069
This reputation is reaffirmed in the film's
climactic scene, which involves Darkseid witnessing

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:01.930
Steppenwolf's defeat at the hands of the Justice
League.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:05.710
Shortly afterwards, his second-in-command,
DeSaad, notes that he always knew Steppenwolf

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:06.710
would fail.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.939
But despite this setback, Darkseid has already
got his eyes set on the future.

00:06:09.939 --> 00:06:13.789
Now knowing that the Anti-Life Equation is
built into the planet, Darkseid intends to

00:06:13.789 --> 00:06:17.009
pursue Earth again, this time with more extreme
force.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:20.939
Darkseid references "the armada" and "the
old ways," referring to an earlier flashback

00:06:20.939 --> 00:06:24.999
that showed him leading a massive army to
destroy Earth, just as he had done with thousands

00:06:24.999 --> 00:06:26.309
of planets before.

00:06:26.309 --> 00:06:30.960
At the time, he was stopped by the combined
forces of Amazonians, Atlanteans, mortal men,

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.740
gods, and a Green Lantern warrior.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.969
Now, he intends to lead such an army again
to Earth to face off against the newly united

00:06:36.969 --> 00:06:37.999
Justice League.

00:06:37.999 --> 00:06:42.129
As Darkseid lurches out of frame in his final
scene in the Snyder Cut, it becomes apparent

00:06:42.129 --> 00:06:46.749
that this moment functions to further solidify
the ruler of Apokolips as a formidable threat

00:06:46.749 --> 00:06:48.520
in a potential Justice League follow-up.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.550
Zack Snyder's Justice League concludes with
an epilogue entitled "A Father Twice Over."

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:58.001
The title refers to a line said by Silas Stone
to his son in a pre-recorded message, where

00:06:58.001 --> 00:07:02.249
he mentions that, through being his biological
father and giving him his robotic enhancements,

00:07:02.249 --> 00:07:04.929
he's Cyborg's father in more ways than one.

00:07:04.929 --> 00:07:08.770
Stone's monologue to his son about the importance
of pursuing your own path in this world plays

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:12.789
over a montage showing where all the members
of the Justice League are in the wake of defeating

00:07:12.789 --> 00:07:14.099
Steppenwolf.

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:17.619
Aquaman meets up with Mera and Vulko, who
are both grateful for this half-Atlantean's

00:07:17.619 --> 00:07:19.280
part in saving the world.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:23.120
Meanwhile, Bruce Wayne uses his enormous wealth
to buy up the bank that foreclosed on Clark

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.960
Kent's childhood farmhouse home.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.169
Barry Allen has also managed to score a job
at a crime lab in his home of Central City,

00:07:29.169 --> 00:07:31.319
much to his incarcerated father's delight.

00:07:31.319 --> 00:07:35.059
Most importantly, though, is that Wayne buys
up a building to serve as a headquarters for

00:07:35.059 --> 00:07:39.089
the Justice League and their activities, complete
with a large round table that, quote, "has

00:07:39.089 --> 00:07:41.169
chairs for six ... but room for more."

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:45.110
Both the building and the table echo the team's
classic Hall of Justice location, and the

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.590
reference to the group expanding its roster
in the future is an acknowledgement of how

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:52.479
so many DC Superheroes have come and gone
from the Justice League in the comics.

00:07:53.479 --> 00:07:57.149
Zack Snyder's Justice League concludes with
a trio of standalone sequences that help to

00:07:57.149 --> 00:07:59.839
set up future adventures for its principal
characters.

00:07:59.839 --> 00:08:03.119
The first of these scenes is one that will
be familiar to anyone who saw the mid-credits

00:08:03.119 --> 00:08:05.399
sequence in the theatrical cut of Justice
League.

00:08:05.399 --> 00:08:09.649
The rendezvous between Lex Luthor and Deathstroke
is retained here and begins like it does in

00:08:09.649 --> 00:08:13.529
the original version, with an Arkham Asylum
guard discovering that Luthor has broken out

00:08:13.529 --> 00:08:14.529
of his cell.

00:08:14.529 --> 00:08:18.340
We then cut to Deathstroke emerging onto the
billionaire's yacht, which is where the Snyder

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.119
Cut differs from the theatrical version.

00:08:20.119 --> 00:08:23.529
Originally, this sequence revolved around
Luther hinting at the formation of the Legion

00:08:23.529 --> 00:08:24.749
of Doom.

00:08:24.749 --> 00:08:32.180
"To put it plainly, shouldn't we have a league
of our own?"

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:36.340
Here, Luthor calls upon Deathstroke — who
harnesses a grudge against Batman — to divulge

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:39.430
the news that Gotham's Dark Knight is actually
Bruce Wayne.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:42.950
It's info that gets the grizzled Deathstroke
to smile and announce that there's reason

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:43.950
to celebrate.

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:47.430
Apparently, this whole scene was meant to
serve as a set-up for Ben Affleck's proposed

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:51.590
solo Batman movie, which would've seen Deathstroke
serve as its principal antagonist.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:55.030
But in the years since this post-credit scene
was filmed, things have changed drastically

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:56.990
for Batman's big-screen plans.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:09:00.910
We know Ben Affleck's character is returning
for The Flash, but past that, we're unsure

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:05.060
of what's in store for the Caped Crusader,
especially with Robert Pattinson running around.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:08.990
However, this initial tease has been restored
in Zack Snyder's Justice League to offer fans

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:12.200
a taste of what could've been and, hopefully,
what can be again.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.520
The second of the Snyder Cut's closing scenes
returns to a familiar locale from Batman v

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:20.450
Superman: Dawn of Justice – Batman's "Knightmare"
landscape.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:25.560
This particular voyage to the post-apocalyptic
location sees Batman joined by a gaggle of

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:30.110
companions, including Justice League members
Flash and Cyborg, Mera, Deathstroke, and Jared

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.190
Leto's Joker.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:34.860
The scene begins with Mera discussing her
desire to murder those responsible for killing

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:39.080
Aquaman before asking Batman how he could
possibly know what it's like to lose a loved

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.080
one.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.190
This leads to a chat between Joker and Batman,
with the former goading the Dark Knight over

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.530
the loss of his parents.

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:48.410
To retort, Batman recalls how he held a dying
Harley Quinn in his arms while she said to

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:49.420
kill the Joker.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:53.160
These conflict-ridden allies are suddenly
greeted by a figure from Batman's previous

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.880
Knightmare experience — an evil, twisted
version of Superman.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:01.050
Now working for Darkseid, this Superman fires
laser beam blasts from his eyes at the team

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:04.500
before Bruce Wayne suddenly awakens in the
present day from his vision.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.790
Not only does this closing sequence follow
up on threads and characters from prior DCEU

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:12.590
movies, but it's also a glimpse at what Zack
Snyder once envisioned for the franchise's

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.590
future.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.650
According to Snyder, Justice League 2 would've
been largely set within this Knightmare landscape.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:22.060
While that follow-up remains an unlikely proposition,
this closing scene in the Snyder Cut offers

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.510
a glimpse of what could've been.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:28.630
With Zack Snyder's Justice League, die-hard
fans of the DCEU finally got to see Harry

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:34.190
Lennix's Man of Steel character, Calvin Swanwick,
reveal himself as the superhero Martian Manhunter.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:38.750
Fans had long suspected Swanwick's identity,
and the rumor was finally confirmed by Snyder

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:39.750
in 2019.

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.380
However, it seemed destined to become an obscure
"what if" scenario.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.810
But with the release of the Snyder Cut, the
casting became a reality.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:49.880
This big reveal is first realized in the movie
through an earlier moment where Martian Manhunter

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.820
takes on the form of Ma Kent to encourage
Lois Lane.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:57.210
The extraterrestrial superhero then returns
in the very last scene of the entire film.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:00.920
This sequence begins with Bruce Wayne, shaken
awake from a Knightmare vision, walking out

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.440
of his house to see Martian Manhunter floating
above.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:07.290
The otherworldly hero notes that he and Wayne
are both aware that Darkseid is not finished

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:08.290
with Earth.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:12.070
With impending doom on the horizon, as well
as being inspired by the Justice League, Martian

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:16.390
Manhunter has decided to engage in superheroics
for the sake of protecting this planet once

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:17.390
again.

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:20.430
The scene concludes with Martian Manhunter
telling Bruce Wayne that his parents would

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:24.140
be proud of him for assembling the Justice
League, and then he reveals his name to the

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.140
billionaire.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:29.380
It's a moment that not only pays off Swanwick's
presence in previous Snyder DCEU movies but

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:34.940
also sets up Martian Manhunter as a potential
participant for any future DCEU efforts.

